# the Jev panel (TUI-DESIGN-2 §4.6): collapsed strip by default after a run (`▸ jev s<N> · <n> decisions`); /panel opens it
# (`▾ decisions` header, ≤ 6 rows, the `… <n> more rows · /panel full expands` row); /panel off collapses it again (§8.2 panel.steps)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.3
send make the tests pass
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[run\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* start 
expect finished [·-] (complete|max_steps|generator_done)
expect ▸(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* jev s\d+ · \d+ decisions
expect Follow-up, question
send /panel
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect ▾(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* decisions
expect more rows
send /panel off
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect ▸(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* jev
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
